## LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working tree. Plain `text=auto` would
## leave the checkout to core.autocrlf, which is true on this machine, so the
## editor would write the LF that .editorconfig asks for and git would hand back
## CRLF on the next checkout - a phantom diff on every file, forever. The only
## exception is further down: batch files, which genuinely want CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

## Source
*.cs        text diff=csharp
*.csx       text diff=csharp
*.md        text diff=markdown
*.json      text
*.xml       text
*.yml       text
*.yaml      text
*.editorconfig text

## MSBuild and solution files
*.csproj    text
*.props     text
*.targets   text
*.slnx      text
*.sln       text eol=crlf

## Scripts. These must agree with the end_of_line rules in .editorconfig, or
## every save fights the checkout normalisation.
## PowerShell is LF: pwsh reads either, and the scripts run on Linux in CI.
## Batch is CRLF: cmd.exe can behave differently reading a label or a goto
## target that ends with a bare LF.
*.ps1       text eol=lf
*.psm1      text eol=lf
*.psd1      text eol=lf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.sh        text eol=lf

## Binary - never diff, never normalise
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.7z        binary
*.dll       binary
*.exe       binary
*.pdb       binary
*.snk       binary
*.pfx       binary

## Audio fixtures used by tests must survive byte identical.
*.mp3       binary
*.m4a       binary
*.aac       binary
*.wav       binary
*.flac      binary
*.ogg       binary
*.opus      binary
*.ts        binary

## HLS playlists are text fixtures, but their exact bytes matter to the parser,
## so keep them LF everywhere rather than letting Windows rewrite them.
*.m3u8      text eol=lf

## Keep generated and vendored files out of language stats and diffs.
*.g.cs              linguist-generated=true -diff
*.Designer.cs       linguist-generated=true -diff
**/obj/**           linguist-generated=true
**/bin/**           linguist-generated=true
